From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 15:25:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hotdog: add a capture front end

MultiMedia1 is currently the only Q6ASM front end, so playback and capture
have to share one PCM. That does not work in practice. A capture stream on
this card is only openable once the front end is joined to SLIMBUS_0_TX,
and a sound server probes the PCM before it applies any use-case sequence,
so the probe fails and the whole card is rejected rather than just the
microphone.

Add MultiMedia2 as a second front end and give it its own DAI link, so
playback stays on PCM 0 and capture gets PCM 1. This matches how other
SM8150 boards with this codec describe the split.

The back ends are unchanged: playback still reaches the speakers through
QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX and the headphone path through SLIMBUS_6_RX, while
capture continues to use the existing SLIMBUS_0_TX to AIF1_CAP link.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-oneplus-hotdog.dts
@@ -380,6 +380,10 @@
 	dai@0 {
 		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA1>;
 	};
+
+	dai@1 {
+		reg = <MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>;
+	};
 };

 &sound {
@@ -404,6 +408,14 @@
 		};
 	};

+	mm2-dai-link {
+		link-name = "MultiMedia2";
+
+		cpu {
+			sound-dai = <&q6asmdai MSM_FRONTEND_DAI_MULTIMEDIA2>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	speaker-dai-link {
 		link-name = "Speaker Playback";

--
2.50.1
